{% doc %}
  @prompt
    Create a section called “Recently Viewed Products” in the Bonne Soirée style — minimal, elegant, and editorial.
    
    Functionality
    
    Automatically show the last products viewed by the customer (store data in localStorage under recently_viewed).
    
    Keep only 12 handles (most recent first, no duplicates).
    
    Fetch product JSONs from /<locale?>/products/{handle}.js.
    
    Display up to 6 products (editable).
    
    If empty, show a small message “No products viewed yet.” and allow a “Hide when empty” toggle.
    
    Optional “Clear history” link that clears recently_viewed.
    
    Layout
    
    Editable title (“Recently Viewed”) and subtitle.
    
    Alignment control: left / center / right (must work).
    
    Layout option: carousel or grid.
    
    Carousel → desktop 4–6 products, mobile 2–3.
    
    Grid → desktop 3–4 columns, mobile 2 columns.
    
    Each card: product image, title, price (normal font weight, no bold).
    
    Hover → show 2nd image if available or soft shadow.
    
    Clicking opens the product page.
    
    Style
    
    Scoped styles (no need to edit theme CSS).
    
    Typography: Times New Roman, regular, never bold.
    
    Colors: #121212 text, #666 gray, white background.
    
    Cards with 6px radius and soft shadow only on hover.
    
    Minimal arrows and dots (opacity ~0.4 → 0.7 on hover).
    
    Header spacing balanced top & bottom.
    
    Schema settings
    
    heading, subheading, alignment, layout, max_items, show_clear_history, hide_when_empty., Create a section called “Recently Viewed Products” in the Bonne Soirée style — minimal, elegant, and editorial.
    
    Functionality
    
